## Context

Child of 0700. Backward and forward citation search from the ICF works retained
by 1655. Decision of the 29 September consultation: two rounds; a third only if
the second brings admissible works. Rerun conditions: interrupted query, missed
sentinel, external reference without decision, incomplete summary.

Baseline integration closes under 1655. This ticket owns incremental delivery,
pool merge, ICF screening, venue and discipline refresh, and count reconciliation
for its additions, through the existing intake and screening procedures. Screen
each round before measuring its eligible yield and choosing the next frontier.
Keep uncertain works and sentinel routes in the seed roster; the fully graded
REL set alone is not the discovery universe. Execution plan and baseline evidence:
`docs/rel-corpus-completion-2026-10-08.md`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Two rounds run, counts per round (references and citations, duplicates, new works)
- [ ] Third round triggered or dropped, with the measurement that decides it
- [ ] New works delivered under the intake contract with provenance, merged and screened incrementally within 1654; venue/discipline data and counts reconciled before each round's yield is measured

## Raid checkpoint — 1654 — Phase 2 Imagine

The baseline is complete but chaining has not run. Simplest path: a narrow resumable OpenAlex collector plus existing intake/pool/screen/venue/view procedures. Discovery seeds are final ICF icf/unsure and sentinels, not the fully graded REL population: baseline 19,852 seeds, 17,641 OA identities, 2,211 missing OA identities, 6,433 without DOI. Resolve missing IDs or document unresolved routes. Do not replace this discovery population with 7,499 inclusions. Avoid a new harvest framework. Existing metadata resolvers are lossy and existing cursor search is not resumable; reuse HTTP/text/keystore helpers, not their filtered outputs. Archive complete raw payloads and separate seed–candidate edges.


## Raid checkpoint — 1654 — Phase 3 Actions and first test

1. Archive deterministic seed roster, sentinel inclusion reasons and pool/config hashes. Resolve missing OA IDs by batched DOI then evidence-based title/author/year; preserve ambiguous/no-match routes.
2. Add a narrow collector and meaningful tests. Batch backward seed metadata/reference resolution and forward OR-cites queries with cursor paging, no year cap. Request referenced_works in forward payloads; intersect against all query seeds to preserve all edges. Save full raw page before committing next cursor. Resume idempotently; changed query/input basis refuses resume.
3. Export complete metadata/full reconstructed abstracts, all retrieved works including existing-pool/out-of-window works, query/date/pagination registry, exclusions, duplicate-discovery ledger, raw files and all edges. Validate intake. No relevance filtering before pool merge.
4. Meter current OA credits from meta.cost and credit headers, also historical USD headers where present. Current source check: single-entity ID/DOI free; filter/list 1 credit=$0.0001/call; search 10 credits=$0.001/call; free $1/day. Maximum100 OR values/page100; detect exhausted/repeated cursor and complete documented termination. Reconcile monetary charges and free allowance separately. Reserve outstanding-call maximum liabilities against total USD20 before submission, including retries; never restart concurrent abandoned batch and synchronous work blindly.
5. Merge each round via existing pool builder. Reconcile keys using explicit identifiers/member provenance and append-only migration records; ambiguous joins refuse label transfer. Refresh venues/view, run Design B for new or changed unscreened works, import paired labels, then v2 stage2 plus established correction procedures and dimensions. Archive all answers/routes/prompts/costs. A new small generalized v2 paid runner is required: discipline catch-up transport cannot be used unchanged because answer writer/parser are discipline-only.
6. Measure eligible research works and observed families only after screening/venue/dimension reconciliation; separately report retrieved records, unique candidates, overlap, genuinely new works, metadata enrichment, ICF/unsure routes and unresolved/pending works. Advance from newly admissible retained works with uncertain/sentinel discovery routes kept as protocol requires.
7. Run two rounds; trigger third if round2 yields admissible works; continue if protocol closure requires further chaining. Interrupted queries, missed sentinels, external references without decision, incomplete summaries or pending new-work decisions do not support saturation/closure. Budget exhaustion checkpoints incomplete work and does not close1654.
8. DVC-push immutable delivery/screen/venue/run artifacts, report stopping decision, then required populated padme gate and PR.

First red test: one mocked forward result cites two query seeds; assert one delivered work and two distinct edges, complete abstract, no year filter. A first-seed-only association must fail. Add meaningful interruption/resume and unresolved-identity coverage.

Verified reusable signatures/CLI:
- pipeline_io.retry_get(url, params=None, headers=None, delay=0.2, max_retries=…, timeout=60, counters=None, backoff_base=2.0, jitter_max=1.0).
- pipeline_keystore.read_credential(provider, source, *, keys_dir=None); OpenAlex and OPENROUTER_API_KEY_CLIMATEFINANCE present, generic OPENROUTER_API_KEY absent. Never log keys.
- reconstruct_abstract from openalex_corpus.text (utils facade also exports); NOT pipeline_text.
- corpus_rel_pool.run(cfg,catalogue_path,intake_dir,out_dir).
- corpus_icf_stage1_input.run(pool_path,table_path,output,priority,rule,exclude_inputs=None); CLI --output/--exclude-input.
- corpus_icf_stage1_designb.py --input … --output-dir … --budget-usd …; cumulative run-directory cap. corpus_icf_import.py --output TABLE stage1-designb --run-dir … --pool ….
- corpus_icf_stage2.py build --output-dir …; parse --chunk-dir … --model … --run-id … --machine … --suffix … --prompt config/rel_stage2_prompt_v2.md.
- enrich_rel_venues_openalex.fetch_batch(ids,api_key); CLI --pool/--output/--budget-floor.


## Raid checkpoint — 1654 — Phase 4 feasibility: WARN, feasible with corrections

All named existing paths/CLI verified. Full v2 execution adapter and safe generic rekey mapping remain implementation. Existing resolve_openalex_ids strips abstracts; catalog_rel_sud_search.slim truncates to1500; neither is full metadata archival. Planning source checks made no paid calls. Count actual git paths before execute: target ≤14 including ticket/tests/DVC pointers/.gitignore; if15+, split scoped implementation/delivery PRs via child tickets without weakening scientific closure. No Makefile/shared pipeline edits needed.

